<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Protective Division of Quito</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1820</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as División Protectora de Quito</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Protective Division of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> was the army raised by the Free Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guayaquil">Guayaquil</a> after its declaration of independence in October 1820 to free the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-ecuador">Ecuadorian highlands</a> from Spanish rule. After early successes it was defeated at Huachi in November 1820, and the liberation of Quito was later completed with help from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-jose-de-sucre">Antonio José de Sucre</a>.</p></div>
